Problem: Given a set of points in 2D space, find the smallest circle that encloses all the points.
Solution: The problem can be solved using the concept of convex hull and group theory. The convex hull of a set of points is the smallest convex polygon that encloses all the points. The smallest circle that encloses all the points is the circumcircle of the convex hull.

